<title>BELGIUM: GBL DECLINES COMMENT ON SUEZ STAKE REPORT.</title>
<headline>GBL DECLINES COMMENT ON SUEZ STAKE REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Groupe Bruxelles Lambert (GBL) declined to comment on a report in French daily Agefi which said the group had bought a one percent stake in Compagnie de Suez from French insurer UAP.</p>
<p>The paper said the purchase by Belgian financier Albert Frere -- head of GBL -- appeared aimed at securing a seat on the Suez board.</p>
<p>On October 7, GBL's Electrafina unit bought Elf Aquitaine's 2.9 percent stake in Suez.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
